UPPER() and LOWER() Functions

The UPPER() and LOWER() functions are used to change the case of text.

1. UPPER() Function

The UPPER() function is used to convert text into uppercase letters.

Syntax:

UPPER(string)

Example:

SELECT UPPER('this is convert into upper case');

Output:
THIS IS CONVERT INTO UPPER CASE


2. LOWER() Function

The LOWER() function is used to convert text into lowercase letters.

Syntax:

LOWER(string)

Example:

SELECT empName, LOWER(empName)
FROM employee_info;

Explanation:
This converts all employee names from the empName column into lowercase letters.

Example:

SELECT LOWER('HELLO VAIBHAV');

Output:
hello vaibhav


Key Point:

UPPER() → Converts text to UPPERCASE.

LOWER() → Converts text to lowercase.
